Problem Statement
Create:
1.	An abstract class Appliance with:
o	Fields: brand (String), powerConsumption (double)
o	Abstract method: void turnOn()
2.	Three subclasses:
o	WashingMachine
o	Refrigerator
o	Microwave
Each subclass provides its own implementation of turnOn().
3.	In the main() method:
o	Create one object of each subclass.
o	Call their turnOn() methods to print the brand name and power consumption.
Requirements
•	Use abstract keyword for the base class.
•	Override the abstract method in all subclasses.
•	Display meaningful output for each appliance.
•	Demonstrate runtime polymorphism by calling methods via superclass references (optional).
